Benchmark viewer patch for HP2-SLAM (upstream 5f33946), applied after
hp2slam_no_debug_leftovers.patch to the installed hp2_slam package. It
changes only the Open3D live view; the estimate is unchanged:
  - the camera is free by default, like RViz (mouse: left-drag rotates,
    Ctrl+left-drag or middle-drag pans, the wheel zooms); F cycles
    free -> follow -> topdown (the author's modes, which re-centre on the
    current pose every scan);
  - the finished local maps are drawn in grey at their current key poses,
    so the whole map is visible and moves with loop closures;
  - the view's bounds grow with the map (Open3D limits zooming out to them)
    while the camera stays where it is;
  - loop closures are drawn in red (the author's list was never filled);
  - ESC/Q or closing the window closes the viewer only; the author's
    os._exit(0) ended HP2-SLAM without writing any result.

